+# Epic Story Breakdown: Capture and review
+
+**Epic**: E001 - Capture and review  
+**Project**: 001-pulseboard  
+**Created**: 2026-08-10  
+**Version**: 1.0  
+**Status**: Draft
+
+---
+
+## 📊 Information Sources
+
+**Traceability**: This breakdown was created from:
+
+- **Required Inputs**:
+  - `epic.md` — transcript capture, action review, explicit confirmation, and workspace isolation.
+  - `epic-tech-spec.md` — workspace-scoped storage and reads, asynchronous extraction, and confirmation fields/audit data.
+- **Recommended Inputs**:
+  - `epic-codebase-scan*.md` — not present.
+  - `PRD.md` / `context.md` / `architecture.md` — not present.
+  - Epic and project constitutions — not present.
+
+---
+
+## Summary
+
+**Total Stories**: 3  
+**Epic Dependencies**: None recorded  
+**Estimated Duration**: 3 ordered implementation slices  
+**Parallelization Potential**: Low — each user-visible slice builds on the prior data and review surface.
+
+---
+
+## Story Organization
+
+### Phase 1: Foundation Setup
+
+- [ ] S001 Capture a transcript and generate proposed actions
+  - **Type**: Technical + user-facing foundation
+  - **Details**: Store a submitted transcript under its workspace and start asynchronous proposed-action extraction without treating any result as confirmed.
+  - **References**: `epic.md`; `epic-tech-spec.md`
+  - **Duration**: 1 slice
+
+### Phase 2: Core Review
+
+- [ ] S002 Review and edit proposed actions in the active workspace
+  - **Type**: User story
+  - **Story**: As a facilitator, I want to see and edit proposed actions for the active workspace so that I can prepare them for an intentional confirmation.
+  - **Depends on**: S001
+  - **Technical Approach**: Load only actions belonging to the active workspace and keep edits separate from confirmation.
+  - **References**: `epic.md`; `epic-tech-spec.md`
+  - **Duration**: 1 slice
+
+### Phase 3: Explicit Confirmation
+
+- [ ] S003 Confirm an action explicitly with accountable details
+  - **Type**: User story + integrity boundary
+  - **Story**: As a facilitator, I want to explicitly confirm a reviewed action with its owner and future due date so that the commitment is attributable and never inferred.
+  - **Depends on**: S002
+  - **Technical Approach**: Reject confirmation without text, owner, or a future `due_at`; record the confirmer and timestamp only when the facilitator performs the confirmation action.
+  - **References**: `epic.md`; `epic-tech-spec.md`
+  - **Duration**: 1 slice
+
+### Phase 4: Quality & Polish
+
+- No standalone story. Workspace isolation is an acceptance boundary in S002 and non-implicit, auditable confirmation is an acceptance boundary in S003; separating either would make a false "quality-only" slice rather than a shippable behavior.
+
+---
+
+## Story Details
+
+### S001: Capture a transcript and generate proposed actions
+
+**User Story**  
+As a facilitator, I want to upload a transcript and receive proposed actions asynchronously so that I have a draft to review without treating extraction as confirmation.
+
+**Acceptance Criteria**:
+- `AC-1`: A submitted transcript is stored under its workspace and starts asynchronous proposed-action extraction.
+- `AC-2`: Extracted actions remain proposed, not confirmed.
+
+**Technical Implementation (high level)**:
+1. Accept a transcript with its workspace context.
+2. Persist the transcript and extraction output under `workspace_id`.
+3. Run extraction asynchronously and expose proposed actions for later review.
+
+**Test Coverage**:
+- Integration: a workspace-scoped submission produces proposed actions without confirmation.
+
+### S002: Review and edit proposed actions in the active workspace
+
+**User Story**  
+As a facilitator, I want to see and edit only the active workspace's proposed actions so that I can prepare the right actions safely.
+
+**Acceptance Criteria**:
+- `AC-1`: The review UI loads proposed actions only for the active workspace.
+- `AC-2`: The facilitator can edit a proposed action before confirmation.
+
+**Technical Implementation (high level)**:
+1. Query proposed actions with active `workspace_id` as a required boundary.
+2. Render the scoped review list.
+3. Persist edits while preserving the proposed state.
+
+**Test Coverage**:
+- Integration: actions from another workspace cannot appear in the active workspace review UI.
+
+### S003: Confirm an action explicitly with accountable details
+
+**User Story**  
+As a facilitator, I want to confirm an action explicitly with all required details so that a real commitment is recorded only when I choose it.
+
+**Acceptance Criteria**:
+- `AC-1`: Confirmation requires action text, an owner, and a future `due_at`.
+- `AC-2`: A successful explicit confirmation records the confirmer and confirmation timestamp.
+- `AC-3`: Extraction and editing alone never confirm an action.
+
+**Technical Implementation (high level)**:
+1. Offer a distinct confirmation operation for a reviewed action.
+2. Validate all required confirmation fields, including a future due date.
+3. Record the actor and timestamp atomically with the state transition.
+
+**Test Coverage**:
+- Integration: invalid or implicit paths cannot confirm; an explicit valid path records the audit data.
+
+---
+
+## Execution Strategy
+
+### Parallel Execution Groups
+
+None. S002 requires S001's transcript/proposal boundary, and S003 depends on the review/edit contract from S002. Parallel implementation would risk inventing incompatible action states.
+
+### Critical Path
+
+S001 → S002 → S003 → Complete
+
+### Resource Allocation
+
+- Phase 1: 1 developer
+- Phase 2: 1 developer
+- Phase 3: 1 developer
+
+---
+
+## Dependencies
+
+### External Dependencies
+
+- No external service or library dependency is specified in the available epic artifacts.
+
+### Inter-Story Dependencies
+
+| Story | Depends On | Provides To |
+|------|------------|-------------|
+| S001 | — | S002 |
+| S002 | S001 | S003 |
+| S003 | S002 | — |
+
+---
+
+## Risk Mitigation
+
+| Story | Risk | Mitigation |
+|------|------|------------|
+| S001 | Extraction could be mistaken for a commitment. | Keep every extracted action in the proposed state. |
+| S002 | A review read could cross workspace boundaries. | Require the active `workspace_id` for reads and cover cross-workspace exclusion. |
+| S003 | A partial or background action could be confirmed implicitly. | Use a dedicated confirmation operation with required-field validation and audit data. |
+
+---
+
+## Definition of Done
+
+Per Story:
+- [ ] Code implemented and reviewed
+- [ ] Unit tests passing
+- [ ] Integration tests passing
+- [ ] Documentation updated (as applicable)
+- [ ] Acceptance criteria verified
+
+Epic Complete:
+- [ ] All stories done
+- [ ] Workspace isolation proven on the review path
+- [ ] Explicit-confirmation invariants proven
+
